1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:02,600
(Penny:)Sheldon?

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:04,640
(Leonard:)Hello.

3
00:00:04,640 --> 00:00:05,640
(Penny:)What are you doing here?

4
00:00:05,640 --> 00:00:08,040
(Sheldon:)I have troubles, Penny.

5
00:00:08,040 --> 00:00:09,640
(Sheldon:)I've come to pour them out

6
00:00:09,640 --> 00:00:12,180
(Sheldon:)to the sympathetic ear
of the local barkeep.

7
00:00:12,180 --> 00:00:14,450
(Penny:)You know, they have
a really nice bar

8
00:00:14,450 --> 00:00:16,320
(Penny:)over at the Olive Garden.

9
00:00:16,320 --> 00:00:18,450
(Sheldon:)I don't like the Olive Garden.

10
00:00:18,450 --> 00:00:20,890
(Sheldon:)They treat me like family.

11
00:00:22,520 --> 00:00:24,620
(Penny:)Okay, Sheldon.
What can I get you?

12
00:00:24,630 --> 00:00:25,890
(Sheldon:)Alcohol.

13
00:00:25,890 --> 00:00:28,190
(Penny:)Could you be
a little more specific?

14
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:29,860
(Sheldon:)Ethyl alcohol.

15
00:00:29,860 --> 00:00:32,070
(Penny(pouring out a shot of tequila):)40 milliliters.

16
00:00:32,070 --> 00:00:34,470
(Penny:)I'm sorry, honey.
I don't know milliliters.

17
00:00:34,470 --> 00:00:37,240
(Sheldon:)Ah. Blame President James
"Jimmy" Carter.

18
00:00:37,240 --> 00:00:40,370
(Sheldon:)He started America on a path
to the metric system

19
00:00:40,370 --> 00:00:42,080
(Sheldon:)but then just gave up.

20
00:00:42,080 --> 00:00:45,140
(Sheldon:)He wonders why he
was a one-term president.

21
00:00:45,150 --> 00:00:47,680
(Penny(pouring out a shot of tequila):)Would you say that's
about 40 milliliters?

22
00:00:47,680 --> 00:00:49,920
(Sheldon:)More or less.
Great.

23
00:00:51,350 --> 00:00:53,020
(Penny:)Now, where were we?

24
00:00:53,020 --> 00:00:56,120
(Sheldon:)I believe you were about
to ask me to choose a cocktail.

25
00:00:56,120 --> 00:00:59,490
(Sheldon:)Fortunately, thanks
to computer-savvy alcoholics,

